{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.617431Z","id":"dd7075fa5f929244d5734ff7b6d76f0e2e79bbdc08fbe31bcaa51c731df49d45","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":503},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","tags":["people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.617749Z","id":"a6c28a8c3821d7360e125842d6084e792ebbdf05c1475349ef768b86551a9ff0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":998},"end":{"line":998},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.617915Z","id":"b8250f201f01ec1fe3c8e24e8d28587286e6593244b49298c3384596e736a28e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/audit.rs:324-333, record f2075a16.\n\nThe extractor's own job costs one interactive round trip before the handler's. Measured with a scratch test against TestServer (debug build, 4 runtime workers, 300-400 sequential requests, three rounds): GET /api/_test/audit/ctx, which is only the extraction, p50 201-227 us against /healthz 144-157 us at idle (about 60 us per job); with 8 clients looping on GET /api/viewers/me, a one-job route at p50 411-420 us, p95 557-566 us, and the extraction alone p50 426-445 us, p95 572-1316 us, so each audited write pays about one more queue wait. Agent tool calls also add one writer transaction for tool.call and, under Claude Code, one for tool.call_id, read-only tools and each wait_for_feedback included. The perf gates passed on unchanged budgets (docs/verification.md §10). Not fixed in the branch's final round: 23 handlers in seven route modules (artifacts, assets, docs, feedback, live, sites, threads, plus the live refile context) take AuditCtx, each with its own job structure, so moving the resolve into their jobs is a change to every audited route rather than a cheap one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":324},"end":{"line":333},"content_hash":"fde9f6c59006fc734d792edc237fec3e153f53108171e787e2ff1539a90cf319"},"suggested_fix":"Take DeferredAudit in the handlers and resolve it inside the handler's own store job, as the session routes already do with for_session.","summary":"Every request that records an event now takes two interactive store jobs: the AuditCtx extractor resolves the actor in its own store_call before the handler's","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.618046Z","id":"d5b8f79e902a51fb14ffb501f131430e3f7a3c20bc1cd0dc11771b67087e965c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/extension.rs:219-225, record e63a6a28.\n\nAdmitting /api/questions and /api/inbox for the extension credential with Rule::Any widens the extension's live-only posture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-chrome-overlay-design.md section 9.5). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:902-915 lists what it lets the extension see and states this is an open owner question. Decision needed: keep this, or restore the live-only posture by filtering /api/inbox and /api/questions to live-page items for the extension, leaving out other items' artifact, and refusing the item and question routes for items that are not live.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"42fd645df0331ac3b918c79febc1ed9c76e9816106613f5ffb3ce2598683cf75"},"summary":"The extension, acting as the owner, may list and read every inbox item and question, gallery artifacts' included","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.618162Z","id":"0a1a0d4b04504252c8f9703038c055b7e0ee47f052ebc29bf8a1458c77a32cd3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:28-31, record 0bcf4f58.\n\nA LAN viewer (the clax_viewer cookie) can create viewers, threads, comments, sends and db documents without limit. Decision needed: add rate limits for LAN writes, and at what rates.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"9a53d622c5cd382d1f2001c30cabb62990539edb252653358aeb36f3bb3ab7e4"},"summary":"LAN viewers' writes have no rate limit","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.618250Z","id":"c685963278cbdc55e58d7e3b5086c00a8cb08e9f8adff1b4436ded2e1c52847e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/identity.rs:496-503, record f3b6a110.\n\nIdentity::caller makes the token an OwnerAgent whenever a session is named (path or X-Clax-Session), known or not; audit_actor records an agent only for a known session of the token's, the agent marker, or x-clax-via mcp, else the owner. Measured through GET /api/_test/audit/ctx: Authorization Bearer + X-Clax-Session 01JB9S00000000000000000099 (no session) and X-Clax-Session not-a-ulid both give {\"type\":\"owner\"}. Today's clients send the marker, so this bites only an older or third-party agent side; it breaks audit spec section 5.2's rule that one request is never an agent to Caller and the owner to the journal.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":503},"content_hash":"e518245782ac10f00f2b65f20d7c675055af73af8c7fb3c52ec0df3ab6eb723b"},"suggested_fix":"When the token names any session that is not known, record the sessionless agent (channel as named, else mcp) instead of the owner; add the case to the_agent_channel_marker_makes_the_token_an_agent.","summary":"The token naming an unknown or non-ULID session without the agent marker is recorded as the owner, while Caller counts it as OwnerAgent","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/viewer.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:50.635550Z","id":"ca958e058f0cec86571d1f0f99a56994639f6be29eef5489eaaf390a72438e8d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/viewer.rs:106-121, record 96c44912.\n\nA Clax-Grant caller writing a thread or a comment without author_kind agent is attributed to its grant's person (author_public_id, display name), as the token's agents are to the owner. Storing it as an agent comment with its session would show it as the agent's in the shell, but a thread's first comment is a viewer comment (NewThread) and a viewer comment forwards the thread, so the semantics would change. Authorship, which the filter needs, is right either way.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"e1def51929c14fd1c99fd4ce1be5af13d57093d7b469bb09c77918167b711764"},"summary":"A person's agent's viewer-kind comment is stored as its person's viewer comment, not as an agent comment","tags":["revisit:when the shell shows which agent wrote a person's comment","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:51.607040Z","id":"43f3587f33a5bc8686e280aa05b0c01ea11d74aae762de580f6a35419317666d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b8250f201f01ec1fe3c8e24e8d28587286e6593244b49298c3384596e736a28e","summary":"Narrowed, not fixed: b24b98e0 folds the feedback poll's audit context (audit::session_ctx) into its first view's store call and a person's agent's path-artifact right into the caller's own store call, so a person's agent's poll takes three store jobs before answering (four before) and its threads read two (three before). The AuditCtx extractor this record names is unchanged in the 23 audited handlers.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:58:51.609816Z","id":"0bdaf4227e9afdc85ef92df2437f789bc2acb865095b157df6defbdcb4e97c0e","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d5b8f79e902a51fb14ffb501f131430e3f7a3c20bc1cd0dc11771b67087e965c","summary":"35cec880 admits GET /api/approvals/requests for the extension credential (Rule::Any, as spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §15 names: the panel's count and links). Request views carry author, artifact, thread, count and state, never the withheld content, for gallery artifacts too, so this widens the live-only posture in the same way as /api/inbox and /api/questions. Deciding, approving, revoking, GET /api/approvals and every /api/people route stay refused (the_allowlist_names_each_route_and_the_artifact_it_needs_live; api_people::the_extension_lists_the_owners_approval_requests_and_decides_nothing). The decision this record asks for is unchanged and still the owner's; if the owner restores the live-only posture, this route needs the same filtering.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.000502Z","id":"a4dcc4d479fc9e512f8c651968db3ca7dd2f3f9888fd623c01eb776dcf87c6b3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":531},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"dd7075fa5f929244d5734ff7b6d76f0e2e79bbdc08fbe31bcaa51c731df49d45","tags":["people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
