{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.447684Z","id":"d8d034493ea2c2aea6af0f57bcdd2540a6bacfd118ffe6809b6a1bbefcfde5e1","body":{"detail":"gather reads the delivery from Store::session_signals and checks only that the thread is still on its artifact. A person's agent had that thread delivered, so it already knows both IDs, but if the owner narrows its rights afterwards (crates/clax-server/tests/api_where_to_ask.rs a_persons_agent_is_never_shown_a_page_it_may_not_read covers only the page) GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask still names them in where. Gating would make gather async or take the delivery's readability as an argument.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":79},"end":{"line":98},"content_hash":"f25880586c1436d61a2833b2e80ac2ce37d8991b7ea59cb8c2677979f19f79c4"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the delivery's artifact through Agent::named_artifact in clax_http::surface::page's caller and drop the delivery's place when it fails.","summary":"The last delivery's artifact and thread are not passed through the agent's gate (Agent::named_artifact), unlike the page","supersedes":"6487de15515aa1b2986663bfee251b3726ab2a1d700ea3af2b0fcbb666fafb77","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.471032Z","id":"bc165d9a937d392eff78f7eee7a3b57eb023676226cbe49ca1e626540e975bde","body":{"detail":"clax_http::surface::gather sets Signals.artifact_id to the gated page, else the last delivery's artifact, so clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs) places a suggestion whose delivery is older than the last prompt on that artifact rather than on nothing. Not taken: preferring the delivery's artifact over the page, or leaving artifact_id as the page alone (the delivery then places nothing once a prompt is newer).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"9dbf23e2cd1b2790cf84c21e6f34061d651c1c6f1d92cfc4ef7b215cf572b78d"},"summary":"With no page, the delivery's artifact stands in as the session's page; a page, when there is one, wins over an older delivery's artifact","supersedes":"19828f45103bb56569db35d0908af2cee3eab1f3d1611bc2c184e572c94f131e","tags":["revisit:a session's page and its last delivery's artifact differ and questions land on the wrong one","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.619225Z","id":"108dbaa500c4da33d12a3dfffd98697bbfae42767d413350a1172fa1ee186ab9","body":{"detail":"gather sets panel_open from Hub::holds_panel and folds it into clax_open, so an open panel only makes a Clax question showable (and adds 'The extension's panel is open.' to the why). The panel reports no focus or input, so it never gives clax_at: a person reading and typing in the panel looks, to suggest, like a person with no Clax activity, and a panel left open in a background window counts the same as one in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"4e0b3148accd76f7291f85c2f945e73bd9fba891f230599145d21b01e3d8f7eb"},"suggested_fix":"Have the panel report focus and last input as tabs do (the presence report's fields), and count it as engagement on the session's page.","summary":"The extension's side panel counts only as Clax being able to show a question; its focus is unknown","tags":["engagement","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.299679Z","id":"0fc5b5a306904dd9f8d626833098b4c83ea8833e4bd8268df25b8d34ae714499","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:503-503, record fced511a.\n\napi_agent_auth::the_extractor_refuses_a_persons_agent_on_an_owner_agents_route now asserts that every Filtered need in ROUTES is live. The not_yet branches (agent.rs Agent<N> extraction and the body gate) stay for a Filtered route added later; remove them, with FILTERED_LIVE, once no task plans one.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":541},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"e07bad372e55913af9df7b2c800d2741a700fd885fb02cc043d3e30bf32f99fd"},"summary":"Every Filtered need is now in FILTERED_LIVE, so the 503 not_yet path serves no route","supersedes":"a4dcc4d479fc9e512f8c651968db3ca7dd2f3f9888fd623c01eb776dcf87c6b3","tags":["people","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.322058Z","id":"9b2312dfb677c9c5e21ef1ed722dbbb403f86b50dc1b6a39d0c1ccbb0cf57518","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/agent.rs:998-998, record 3c0ad45d.\n\nEvery handler of agent::ROUTES now takes Agent<N> (GET /api/artifacts/{aid}, threads, docs, comment, resolve...). For a request with a clax_viewer cookie, Identity::quick_caller returns None and resolve() reads the viewer row on the blocking pool to tell Person from Viewer. The owner's browser (owner cookie) and the token take the quick path. The extra read is one primary-key lookup per request; it was not measured against scripts/perf-daemon-budget.json.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:27b591eb5eb290f789cd5f959845f6d1064768a7","span":{"start":{"line":1141},"end":{"line":1141},"content_hash":"0084401cde97b2431fc0a50fda577f15da02d5950c956b6bd243c5b7d069ce7d"},"summary":"Agent<N> resolves the full Caller, so a LAN viewer's cookie request on an agent route costs a store read it did not before","supersedes":"562268fb9ae36e1ba471d4da561f1cc0ea0fbea5465e45ef5caf043226acb748","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025601Z","id":"af554733a7d03b01fa2802e9f27141b33c675fb834dfba710abb2887ea730f3e","body":{"detail":"note_poll infers a terminal turn start (Store::note_turn_start, crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs:142-172) at the first non-stop_hook poll after a Stop with no delivery since. Before the session's first Stop nothing is inferred, so the first turn of a session counts only when it ends; a tier=queue poll is the daemon's push claim, not the agent's own activity, so it infers nothing. Inferring the first turn at the session's first poll would show it sooner, at the cost of counting a session a Clax delivery started.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":259},"content_hash":"702ab9b7fcf19eafd968876568876edface6b8b08f79a5a5cf1d78bf5be96c5e"},"summary":"Infer a Codex or Grok turn start only after a reported Stop, and never from a Codex queue poll","tags":["revisit:Codex or Grok sessions are seen whose first turn the suggestion misses","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025950Z","id":"37b666d4f36776fb8128b79924cb3917641e94cab1819ccb8392e76f3574985f","body":{"detail":"gather reads the delivery from Store::session_signals and checks only that the thread is still on its artifact. A person's agent had that thread delivered, so it already knows both IDs, but if the owner narrows its rights afterwards (crates/clax-server/tests/api_where_to_ask.rs a_persons_agent_is_never_shown_a_page_it_may_not_read covers only the page) GET /api/sessions/{id}/where-to-ask still names them in where. Gating would make gather async or take the delivery's readability as an argument.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"419cfefe19db576423e0da9cb5ac40a2ee0db9634d0824303d0fb03b3ec66ef6"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the delivery's artifact through Agent::named_artifact in clax_http::surface::page's caller and drop the delivery's place when it fails.","summary":"The last delivery's artifact and thread are not passed through the agent's gate (Agent::named_artifact), unlike the page","supersedes":"d8d034493ea2c2aea6af0f57bcdd2540a6bacfd118ffe6809b6a1bbefcfde5e1","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.050264Z","id":"67fa6319238a58346033b48df9aafc46f4ab2b9984630b26c353b6a5b27df8cc","body":{"detail":"gather sets panel_open from Hub::holds_panel and folds it into clax_open, so an open panel only makes a Clax question showable (and adds 'The extension's panel is open.' to the why). The panel reports no focus or input, so it never gives clax_at: a person reading and typing in the panel looks, to suggest, like a person with no Clax activity, and a panel left open in a background window counts the same as one in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"4e0b3148accd76f7291f85c2f945e73bd9fba891f230599145d21b01e3d8f7eb"},"suggested_fix":"Have the panel report focus and last input as tabs do (the presence report's fields), and count it as engagement on the session's page.","summary":"The extension's side panel counts only as Clax being able to show a question; its focus is unknown","supersedes":"108dbaa500c4da33d12a3dfffd98697bbfae42767d413350a1172fa1ee186ab9","tags":["engagement","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.074763Z","id":"dc442316ca02e3f9a5a1795a6a78fb5bd08fe2f98f466118be094932367fa080","body":{"detail":"clax_http::surface::gather sets Signals.artifact_id to the gated page, else the last delivery's artifact, so clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs) places a suggestion whose delivery is older than the last prompt on that artifact rather than on nothing. Not taken: preferring the delivery's artifact over the page, or leaving artifact_id as the page alone (the delivery then places nothing once a prompt is newer).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":124},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"9dbf23e2cd1b2790cf84c21e6f34061d651c1c6f1d92cfc4ef7b215cf572b78d"},"summary":"With no page, the delivery's artifact stands in as the session's page; a page, when there is one, wins over an older delivery's artifact","supersedes":"bc165d9a937d392eff78f7eee7a3b57eb023676226cbe49ca1e626540e975bde","tags":["revisit:a session's page and its last delivery's artifact differ and questions land on the wrong one","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-http/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874336Z","id":"dfb2b94c88eee4da6ce67e07819f0c50bd379ad998386b1f0ace55f13b64fd6a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs serves a draft's files with content_policy(.., None) and sets no ContentPolicySet, so rewrite_artifact_host appends the lockdown (own files under /c/<id>/, the bridge, /_blob/<id>/, connect-src 'none'). Policies only narrow, and the draft's own files are under /c/<id>/, but no test covers a draft page under the lockdown (web/e2e/drafts.spec.ts runs the base's drafts; check it passes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"301b95f7aeb38a56eec2f7d801ccf7abd0a3488b0d981ba06a32525771057917"},"summary":"The base's agent draft pages at /c/<id>/draft/... now get the artifact's lockdown policy appended here, beside the policy their route sets","tags":["drafts","security","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
